      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The Q-Tc interval before and after the treadmill exercise test in 48 normal subjects and 59 patients with coronary heart disease were compared. The Q-Tc interval was shorter in normal group at immediate moment, 2, 4 and 6 minutes after the exercise than before. In the coronary heart disease group, the Q-Tc interval at the same time points as above was longer after exercise compared to pre-exercise. There was no significant difference of exercise-induced Q-Tc changes in silent and symptomatic myocardial ischemia."},
